Office of Global Programs

Dear Student,

Congratulations! I am pleased to inform you that you have been selected as one of this year&rsquo;s recipients of the Beesen Global Travel Fellowship. This award will be made to you in the amount of $5,000 and is only redeemable to aid in your participation in the Columbia in Paris program during the summer 2019, as outlined in your application.

Established to support Columbia undergraduates in pursuit of their academic interests related to France, the Beesen Global Travel Fellowship provides financial assistance to individuals seeking to engage those interests by participating in Columbia in Paris program at Reid Hall. The decision to award you this fellowship was made after a careful review of your application, which revealed an academic interest  to engage with French and Francophone culture, a desire to make the most of the abroad experience, and a willingness to articulate the value of the international experience to the wider Columbia community.

If you choose to accept the award, please complete the following no later than April 4, 2019:

(1) Email Lindsey Schram, your Paris Summer Program Adviser, at {mailto:ls2553@columbia.edu ls2553@columbia.edu} to confirm your participation in the program;

(2) Complete your Confirmation of Participation, available through your {http://ogp.columbia.edu OGP account};

(3) Email me (Scott Carpenter; {mailto:sc2764@columbia.edu sc2764@columbia.edu})  to formally accept the Beesen Travel award. Our office will follow up you on the next steps in the disbursement process.

(4) If you have received or are awarded any additional fellowships or funds at any time to support this summer opportunity, you are required to inform our office immediately. 

Please note, if you cannot accept the award, please contact me by April 4, 2019 with your decision to decline the award.

Congratulations once again!

Best wishes,

Scott Carpenter

Associate Dean, Global Education

Office of Global Programs

Columbia University
